<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65732" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεῖον</span></b>  (B), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lamb</i> or <i>sheep offered at the Athenian
			Apaturia</i> by a father who was enrolling his son among his 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φράτερες, τοῦ μείου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					22.1237.5
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ μεῖα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				60
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρέστησε μεῖον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Is.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					124
				</span></i>
			: expld. by Sch. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				810
			</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Eratosth.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Harp.
			</span></i>) as neut. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μείων</span>, <i>too
				light</i>! from the cry of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φράτερες</span> when the lamb was weighed; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μειαγωγέω</span>.</div>
